  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enterprise Development for Rural Families (EDRF III) - EDRF III</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Enterprise Development for Rural Families (EDRF III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EDRF III has the goal to contribute to reduction of poverty in Kenya through improved livelihoods specifically for women and youth. The intervention has the purpose to support development of profitable micro-enterprises for rural and peri-urban areas targeting the marginalized women, youth, and men. The key problems which the intervention will address within the micro-enterprise development environment as the underlying causes of poverty in the designate counties are: Low access to information; lack of entrepreneurial skills; poor access to markets; and poor access to financial services.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enterprise development for rural families has the goal to contribute to reduction of poverty in Kenya through improved livelihoods. The purpose of the intervention is to support development of profitable enterprises for rural and peri-urban areas targeting the marginalized women, youth, and men. The key problems to be addressed are: i. Low access to information; ii. Lack of entrepreneurial skills; iii. Poor access to markets; and iv. Poor access to financial services</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Enterprise development for rural families has the goal to contribute to reduction of poverty in Kenya through improved livelihoods. The purpose of the intervention is to support development of profitable enterprises for rural and peri-urban areas targeting the marginalized women, youth, and men. The key problems to be addressed are: i. Low access to information; ii. Lack of entrepreneurial skills; iii. Poor access to markets; and iv. Poor access to financial services</narrative>
  </description>
